\pard\qc\sa240\b\f1\fs32\cf2 Savings Account Terms and Conditions\cf0\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\qc\sa240\i\f1\fs18\cf3 Form DEP-TC-003 | Revised January 1, 2026\cf0\i0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb240\sa120\b\f1\fs24 1. Membership and Par Value\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sa160\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 To become a member of Harbor Credit Union you must meet the field of membership requirements in our bylaws and purchase and maintain the par value of one share in a Primary Share Account. The par value of a share is $5.00. If the balance of your Primary Share Account falls below the par value, your membership may be terminated after written notice.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb240\sa120\b\f1\fs24 2. Dividends\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sa160\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Dividends are paid from current income and available earnings after required transfers to reserves. The dividend rate and Annual Percentage Yield on savings accounts are variable and may change at any time as determined by the Board of Directors. Dividends are compounded daily and credited monthly for the Primary Share Account, Youth Savings and Money Market accounts.\par
\pard\s0\sa160\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 You must maintain a minimum daily balance of $100 in your Primary Share Account to earn dividends. If the daily balance is below this amount on any day, no dividends are earned for that day. Harbor uses the daily balance method, which applies a daily periodic rate to the principal in the account each day.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb240\sa120\b\f1\fs24 3. Dividend Period\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sa160\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 The Dividend Period is monthly. For example, the beginning date of the first dividend period of the calendar year is January 1 and the ending date is January 31. All other dividend periods follow the same pattern. If you close your account before dividends are credited, you will receive the accrued dividends through the date of closure.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb240\sa120\b\f1\fs24 4. Transaction Limitations\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sa160\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 You may make an unlimited number of deposits. Harbor limits withdrawals and transfers out of each savings account to six (6) per calendar month by preauthorized, automatic, telephone or online transfer. Transactions in excess of this limit are subject to the excessive withdrawal fee shown below and repeated excess activity may result in the account being converted to a checking account.\par
