\pard\s1\keepn\sb240\sa120\b\f1\fs24 6. Dormant Accounts and Unclaimed Property\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sa160\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 An account with no member-initiated activity for twelve months is classified as dormant. Dormant account fees are listed in the Schedule of Fees and Charges. If an account remains inactive for the period set by state law, Harbor is required to transfer the funds to the state as unclaimed property.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb240\sa120\b\f1\fs24 7. Deposits and Holds\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sa160\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 Funds deposited to savings are available according to the Funds Availability Policy. Harbor may refuse any deposit, limit the amount that may be deposited, or return all or part of a deposit.\par
\pard\s1\keepn\sb240\sa120\b\f1\fs24 8. Governing Law\b0\f0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sa160\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22 These terms are governed by the bylaws of Harbor Credit Union, federal law and regulations, and the laws of the state in which the credit union is chartered. If any provision is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in effect.\par
